-- 0044_import_maintenance_history.sql
-- Import 81 repair events from the "ซ่อมได้" LINE group (10 Dec 2025 – 31 Jul 2026)
-- into the maintenance module, which held nothing at all while seven months of
-- real repair work lived only in a chat thread.
--
-- These are TRANSCRIBED, not reconstructed. Each row keeps the original message
-- verbatim in `problem`, the person who sent it in `reportedBy`, and the date it
-- was sent. Every row says in `notes` that it came from the chat and is not a
-- signed work order, because a record that looks like a work order but was never
-- raised or signed as one is a records-integrity problem in its own right.
--
-- Status is what the chat evidences, nothing more. Only 4 of 81 have a message
-- confirming the repair finished, so 77 import as Open. That is not a claim they
-- are still outstanding today -- a seven-month-old request almost certainly was
-- fixed -- it is a claim that the outcome was never recorded. QA can close them
-- with knowledge; guessing them closed here would manufacture the evidence.
--
-- 22 rows map to a specific asset. 59 do not, and are kept with the machine field
-- empty per QA's decision: the chat says "เครื่องซีล" where the register has six
-- sealers. Dropping them would discard real repair history to avoid an empty
-- field. The reason a row could not be pinned down is written into its notes.
--
-- 33 of those 59 are things absent from the 40-asset register entirely -- water,
-- electrical, doors, trolleys. They are 40% of the actual repair load and the
-- register does not cover them.
--
-- MOLD1 / BELT1 carry the chat's "เครื่องเสียบ L" and "เครื่องหมู L", confirmed
-- by QA as the same machine.

